;;
;; SIBLING to TABLE-STONE-255.71-typed-constructors.edn (AMEND-2's own licensed shape: "append
;; them to the committed table (or a sibling table beside it, said in the SCORE)"). Covers the
;; population the original 177-site corpus census never walked: `wat-scripts/fixes/**`'s own
;; recorded codemods, live wat programs the loader gate type-checks like any other program.
;;
;; 338 rows, one per untyped-constructor call site found by a structural AST walk (the SAME
;; `is-hit?` shape `wat-scripts/fixes/typed-constructors.wat`'s own census logic uses) over the
;; 84 `wat-scripts/fixes/*.wat` files that `wat --check` flagged (measured directly, this resume;
;; the AMEND's own "674 sites" figure double-counted each error — its `grep -c` pattern matched
;; both the CheckError's `:message` and `:reason` fields for the SAME error, so 674 / 2 = 337
;; unique flagged errors; this walk's own site enumeration found one further genuinely-untyped
;; site the wall does not flag at all -- `response-record-to-enum.wat:100:21`, a `Tuple` ctor
;; checked in an ALREADY-expected-type position via `check_tuple_constructor_against` rather than
;; `infer_tuple_constructor`'s bracket-less branch, so it never reaches `untyped_constructor_error`
;; -- typed anyway here for the same "every collection constructor has one shape" consistency the
;; ruling states; 337 + 1 = 338).
;;
;; `line`/`col` key EACH ROW to the call's OWN span (its `(`) -- `typed-constructors.wat`'s own
;; `c69::table-key` convention -- NOT the CheckError's reported span (which for many of these is
;; the call's first ARG, per `untyped_constructor_span`'s documented fallback rule; the two do
;; not coincide and are not meant to).
;;
;; `type` sourced via the STASH-DANCE: the wall's 4 `local_errors.push(untyped_constructor_error
;; (...))` call sites in `src/check.rs` (lines 15692/15797/15965/16551, all inside a `None =>`
;; arm that already "degrades gracefully" -- commenting the push out changes no other control
;; flow) were commented out, `cargo build --release` rebuilt an old-checker binary, and
;; `WAT_CHECK_TYPES=1 wat --check <file>` was run over all 84 files (every one type-checks clean
;; with the wall lifted) to harvest the checker's own recorded type at each site's exact call
;; span. The compact tuple notation `:(A,B)` `format_type_inner` renders (confirmed not directly
;; reader-parseable, matching `typed-constructors.wat`'s own header note) was bridged BY HAND to
;; the parseable `(:wat::core::Tuple :- [A B])` form, recursively, restoring the leading colon a
;; namespaced leaf's compact rendering drops -- 10 distinct raw shapes covered all 337
;; wall-recorded sites (verified: no site's raw type fell outside this set). The one site the
;; type record never reached (`response-record-to-enum.wat:100:21`, a `defn` whose declared
;; return type funnels the constructor's own expected type: the function's signature line 85-86
;; is literally `(:wat::core::HashMap :- [:wat::core::String (:wat::core::Tuple :- [:wat::core::
;; String :wat::core::String])])`) was typed by reading the source directly.
;;
;; `kind` is always `:typed` here -- no STOP-1/legacy-shape/positive-control/removed rows arose in
;; this population; every one of the 338 sites resolved to a concrete type via the stash-dance
;; record or, for the one miss, the enclosing function's own declared signature.
;;
;; Applied by `wat-scripts/fixes/typed-constructors.wat`, same `.typed-constructors-table.edn`
;; side-channel, same stash-dance-free apply pass (the wall's own build is what's restored before
;; applying -- the codemod re-spells `:wat::core::X` primitives to `wat.type/X` at apply time, so
;; this table's `:wat::core::`-spelled `type` strings are its INPUT convention, matching the
